WeightScope - attribution and provenance notes

* All code in this repository was written fresh for WeightScope. No code was
  copied or adapted from other projects.

* dukemawex/secret-loyalties-audit (harness/weight_diff.py) was read as prior
  art. At the commit inspected (7623698, 2026-07-26) that repository has no
  LICENSE file and GitHub reports no license, so none of its code was reused.
  The general idea of ranking tensors by per-tensor L2 change relative to the
  base norm and reading safetensors lazily also appears there; WeightScope's
  implementation (pure numpy, its own safetensors parser, chunked reads,
  hardening, per-layer aggregation) is independent.

* The safetensors parser follows the publicly documented safetensors file
  format (8-byte little-endian header length, JSON header, data offsets).
  The `safetensors` library itself is not used or bundled.

* Runtime dependency (not bundled): NumPy, BSD-3-Clause licence.
